{"hits": {"hits": [{"created": "1996-06-14T00:00:00+00:00", "updated": "2023-03-07T02:21:59.005934+00:00", "links": {"bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2448?format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2448?format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2448?format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2448?format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2448?format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2448?format=cv", "citations": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A2448"}, "id": "2448", "metadata": {"authors": [{"full_name": "Georgi, Howard"}, {"full_name": "Politzer, H.David"}], "publication_info": [{"journal_volume": "9", "page_end": "420", "year": 1974, "page_start": "416", "journal_title": "Phys.Rev.D"}], "texkeys": ["Georgi:1974wnj", "Georgi:1951sr"], "abstracts": [{"value": "We analyze electroproduction in a non-Abelian gauge model of the strong interactions using the techniques of Christ, Hasslacher, and Mueller. The theory is asymptotically free and consistent with scaling up to logarithms. All logarithmic factors appear as inverse powers of ln(\u2212q2) and hence vanish as \u2212q2\u2192\u221e. When \u2212q2 gets very large, the structure functions become strongly peaked near x=0, and as \u2212q2\u2192\u221e approach the singular scaling functions 2xF1(x)=F2(x)=a\u03b4(x), where the constant a is determined. In a strong-interaction model based on the gauge group SU(3) with three triplets of fractionally charged quarks, a=0.16."}], "control_number": 2448, "dois": [{"value": "10.1103/PhysRevD.9.416"}], "titles": [{"title": "Electroproduction scaling in an asymptotically free theory of strong interactions"}], "author_count": 2, "document_type": ["article"]}}], "total": 1}, "links": {"self": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?sort=mostcited&q=j%20Phys.Rev.D%2C9%2C416&size=3&page=1&fields=control_number,title